[statement]
A sticky directory, mode 1777, carrying an access control list. On
extraction GNU tar keeps the sticky bit and bsdtar drops it, leaving a
directory where anyone may remove another's files (measured by extraction).
Strict refuses it; Compatible reads the header's mode, as GNU tar extracts
it.

[archive]
pax SCHILY.acl.access=user::rwx,user:65534:rwx,group::r-x,mask::rwx,other::rwx SCHILY.acl.default=""
header name=d/ typeflag=5 mode=0o1777
header name=after
data "y"
end

[verdict]
strict: refused SpecialBitsWithAcl at 1024
compatible: read

[gnu-tar 1.35]
member listed=d path=d/ size=0 mode=0o1777
member listed=- path=after size=1 mode=0o644 data="y"
exit 0

